<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center" class="tborder" style="border-bottom: 0;">
	<tr class="titlebg">
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="15%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/topic/hot_post.gif" alt="" />
			Author
		</td>
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="85%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			Topic: The Current State of EQ: A Commentary &nbsp;(Read 804 times)
		</td>
	</tr>
</table>
<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="bordercolor">
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=393" title="View the profile of Zerxes">Zerxes</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 46<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I'm a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=393"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=785.msg7487#msg7487"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=785.msg7487#msg7487">Re:The Current State of EQ: A Commentary</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #15 on:</b> April 30, 2004, 05:35:31 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I think this pretty much sums up the current state of EQ - I&#039;ve taken the liberty of doing a Johnny Dangerously-type censorship, otherwise there would be no post after the mods got done censoring it:<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">Man I seriously hope you [insert: language that makes baby Jesus cry] Sony Devs read our board. If your intention with this expansion was to alienate your entire upper tier guild structure across every server then you are succeeding. Old school players are quitting in droves because this expansion is the worse farging, piece of sheet, no quality assured, zero foresight, zero imagination, preschool finger painting quality, craptastic forkwad of an expansion. <br /><br />Not only were the Ikkinz trials completely broken and farging retarded but the initial concept of a specific class needing to get the KS lacks all imagination. Not to mention that it was broken so that you needed first agro and first KS initially. Not to mention that they repopped a new class each time with no farging clue as to whom is the desired class. <br /><br />I&#039;M SORRY YOU CORK SUCKING SONY ICEHOLES BUT MAYBE I DIDN&#039;T GET MY FARGING SECRET SONY DECODER RING SO THAT I COULD UNDERSTAND YOUR LOGIC??? I mean seriously what the fork ever happened to riddles that actually had solvable clues? FORK YOU FORK YOU FORK YOU!!! <br /><br />Now onto Uqua, we have been in this zone for what two or three months now and it has been nerfed and changed like 97 times already and yet it is still unbeatable. Unbeatable because we lack skills? No. Unbeatable because we lack strategies? No. Unbeatable because we can&#039;t get 54 people to log in and do this miserable wretch of a zone? No. It&#039;s unbeatable because yet again THE FARGING SCRIPT IS BROKEN YOU ICEHOLES!!!! <br /><br />I&#039;m sick and farging tired of Beta testing your sheet. Hello Beta is a bad word choice, beta would imply that there was ANY initial testing on your part which clearly is a farging lie. All of this of course leads us to our next possible only other conclusion, and that is that Qvic is not done yet. Just like when Sony told us &quot;The plane of mischief is in game and working as intended&quot; And when we got there about 6 months before any other server guess what - it was unitemized and TOTALLY FORKED UP!! <br /><br />Im sick of your farging lies Sony and this is the last time I will ever play one of your piece of sheet games. The only reason I still log on after 5 farging years is because I owe it to my guildies and friends to see them through this farging piece of sheet expansion. <br /><br />Sony probably puts one dollar into its game for every 1000 it takes in, other wise we might actually have some CS and QA. Greedy farging iceholes. <br /><br />For the record Triton is as far progression wise as any guild in EQ serverwide, this is not a rant this is a well informed fact. So again for the record FORK YOU SONY!! <br /><br />Btw I am in WoW Beta of course, and yes it farging owns you. <br /><br />Lord Mardigann <br />The Vicar <br />TRITON<br /></div><br />&nbsp;:o
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg7493"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=267" title="View the profile of Grem">Grem</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Drolvarg Guardian<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 386<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Officer of Fires of Time<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=267"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=785.msg7493#msg7493"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=785.msg7493#msg7493">Re:The Current State of EQ: A Commentary</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #16 on:</b> April 30, 2004, 06:08:56 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							^^^ <br /><br />That is alot of crying. &nbsp;Sad people.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=472362" target="_blank"><img src="http://flamevault.com/~grem/Grem-1.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg7536"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174" title="View the profile of Delheru">Delheru</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Guild Leader<br />
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 89<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=785.msg7536#msg7536"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=785.msg7536#msg7536">Re:The Current State of EQ: A Commentary</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #17 on:</b> May 02, 2004, 10:51:04 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Well for the most part I definitely agree with it though.<br /><br />For those not in Ikkinz/Uqua, I&#039;ll give you two examples from those zones. Other is obviously just uqua, the other is the Ikkinz raid known as Sanctuary Transcendence (or Ikkinz3).<br /><br /><br />First for Ikkinz.<br />The idea here is fairly straightforward. You fight your way to a room with 4 golems. The golems need to be killed by a certain class, or they will simply respawn. To give a hint of what class is required, they will echo something like &quot;This creature suffers from a acute fear of death&quot; -&gt; Necro.<br /><br />Not the most creative idea ever, but fine. Now what happens in reality?<br /><br />1. People reach it. Whatever you kill, you always get &quot;You need more brawn!&quot;, which supposedly meant warrior or berserker or something? Anyway it never did work.<br />2. We come back since there&#039;s been promised to have been a change. Nothing has changed.<br />3. Now it works on some servers, but not on RN and not a bunch of other servers.<br />4. Some people begin to wonder why the raid is limited to 42 on some servers and to 54 on some others.<br />5. Ok now it &quot;works&quot; on all servers. However instead of the killing blow being critical, what counts is who has initial agro (wtf?)<br />6. The rewards from this wonderful encounter include a pet augment and a 70 ENDURANCE augment, which both rot right off the spot.<br />7. Oops. The golem can change to require a kill by a class not even present in the zone (think berserker). Lets fix that since it apparently annoyed some people.<br />8. RN gets fixed to the 54man limit, but not before a whole bunch of our people has gotten tired of waiting outside and effectively retired.<br />9. Oho something breaks, and the script does not work again for a while.<br />9. THE SCRIPT WORKS! Oh my god.<br />10. The door scripts in Ikkinz bug, and none can go through any doors for a while.<br />11. The creator of the zone feels that the encounter is too easy (what the hell you idiot, it drops trashy loot), and tunes it up.<br /><br />Here is where we are now. There is still constant problems with the door and killing blow recognition scripts being tied to global files apparently, so any patch can break Ikkinz without its creator being aware of it.<br /><br /><br />Ah and Uqua.<br />Zoning in to Uqua, you soon trigger a trap that rushes 4 mobs at you. Quite interesting a concept. There&#039;s later traps that throw 3, 5 or even 6 mobs at you, and usually in lot tighter quarters that the nice open room at zone-in. The few tricks in this zone include:<br />- Anyone dies, a ghost spawns (kos to the raid)<br />- Non-stop AE that is -something to all stats<br />- Ability to reflect the AE with items<br />- Every 120sec or so, the abilities of the mobs in zone get enhanced in two (random) categories<br />- There are AE related traps along the way, that the whole guild sort of has to risk<br /><br />1. Originally yardtrash hits for about 2500, the ghosts for 3500 (hi?) and the ghosts have an unresistable AE of 1500 damage. No guild makes it out of the first room. The ghosts only despawn if agroed for 3 ticks, something which most guilds never realize -&gt; every wipe they have to wait for corpses to pop outside.<br />2. The perma-AE gets toned down, think it was -300 to all originally, but gets cooled down to -250.<br />3. Designer of the zone quits<br />4. The 1500 unresistable AE gets thrown away as ridiculous. The ghosts hit 2500, AND they despawn even when unagroed. Takes 5 ticks or so though.<br />5. Nothing sees invis in the zone, which gets fixed instantly of course.<br />6. People beat the first trap and reach the first AE trap. AE trap instagibs an Ascent raid (I&#039;m sure we weren&#039;t the only ones) to the great amusement of onlookers. AE gets toned down from 7000 unresistable damage, which was pretty harsh on applicant casters.<br />7. The mobs get further toned down a bit.<br />8. Ohos. Golems after the third trap were still hitting for 6900 (lol?), which was somewhat unfair considering deaths DO spawn those ghosts. They get tuned down.<br />9. People reach the first bosses, but mostly by dragging since there are safe spots in the zone.<br />10. Golems you need to kill the first bosses are insta respawn for the whole set, so killing one out of 4 left you with 7 (3 left alive and 4 spawned when you killed one...)<br />11. If a single trap despawns, everything in the zone respawns, which makes it pretty damn hard to add people to the raid due to no CoH. This is considered part of the challenge (f off).<br />12. The respawning traps get fixed, but the doors still lock behind you, so you have to duel people through the door to get them to join you.<br />13. The named are supposed to be killed at once, but most people have trouble killing them with 50ish.<br />14. Oh crap, yeah, they get attack speed bonuses during the whole raid. The hasting effect of staying in zone gets nerfed, and only the +atk one (I believe) remains, this way things are more reasonable.<br />15. Bosses actually die (yay!), now just to kill them both at once.<br />16. The door gets fixed, and it opens now to allow people to join their raids (!)<br />17. The bosses drop worse loot than the first named in Ikkinz1, making this the ultimate risk/reward ever. Fix not in sight.<br />18. You could run from one boss to the other if you were fast. This gets fixed to force splitting of the raid.<br />19. Barxt (the final mob) is in place, but his adds are bit too numerous and nasty. They get tuned down a bit.<br />20. He is almost killed, except the script freezes... That gets fixed.<br />21. Where we are now.<br /><br /><br />The timespan is roughly 2 and a half months here, and for 6 weeks of that we did both of them every 3 days minimum. Shockingly enough some people got frustrated :( &nbsp; I mean no Rathe deja vu or anything, but now it seems they got such a delaying tactic as just another tool in their arsenal.<br /><br />But hey, the content should be sorta ok (except for nonexistant risk vs reward) by the time most guild would reach it =)!!
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg7538"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=214" title="View the profile of Stargazeron">Stargazeron</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 23<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=214"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=785.msg7538#msg7538"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=785.msg7538#msg7538">Re:The Current State of EQ: A Commentary</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #18 on:</b> May 02, 2004, 12:27:39 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I&#039;m not totally sure what the issue was with making Ikkinz3 harder.<br /><br />Altar of Destruction (ikkinz4) was a cakewalk, but they beefed it up... to much imo. &nbsp;Still beatable just a pain in the backside.<br /><br />Biggest problems with Uqua right now I&#039;d say are:<br /><br />#1 - It&#039;s too damn hard to add people to the raid. &nbsp;Nothing like spending half an hour just getting 1 person to the raid.<br /><br />#2 - Pathing still sucks. &nbsp;Quite fun getting an extra mob or two upon triggering a trap.<br /><br />Course we haven&#039;t got to the last guy yet, so I can&#039;t comment on him.<br /><br />The AE deflector item poofing on death/zone is kinda annoying too.<br /><br />Nothing quite as satisfying to tell the raid that they&#039;ve successfully battled through 6 quite nasty traps successfully, and killed one of the mini named in the most difficult accessable zone in EQ, only to get a 70 mana aug, and thats it.<br /><br />I&#039;m told the loot has been tuned a little, but I haven&#039;t seen it.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									&#171; <i>Last Edit: May 02, 2004, 12:28:57 pm by Stargazeron</i> &#187;
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://pages.sssnet.com/stargazer/magelo.html" target="_blank"><img src="http://pages.sssnet.com/stargazer/starsig.jpg" alt="" border="0" /></a>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg7540"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174" title="View the profile of Delheru">Delheru</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Guild Leader<br />
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 89<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=785.msg7540#msg7540"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=785.msg7540#msg7540">Re:The Current State of EQ: A Commentary</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #19 on:</b> May 02, 2004, 12:51:52 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Mostly the issue is risk/reward in transcendence. Take out the rogue dagger and 54 members of Ascent would be equipping the guild up better by farming the 6man ZI mobs in Ikkinz trials.<br /><br />If you want to give reward worthy of a 12 to 18man effort, don&#039;t make us drag more people there.<br /><br /><br /><br />Uqua isn&#039;t that bad anymore. Thing is the wasted effort, which reached quite epic proportions.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
</table>
